    10	//!   * Malformed metadata (any record without '=', including an empty
    11	//!     metadata section) and an unknown or missing `type` silently drop
    12	//!     the request with no response.
    13	//!   * All base64 (payloads and the `mime`, `name`, and `pw` metadata
    14	//!     values) is strict RFC 4648 per the spec's "Encoding of payloads"
    15	//!     section: characters outside the standard alphabet (including
    16	//!     whitespace) and incorrect padding are rejected, never silently
    17	//!     skipped. An invalid value on `wdata` or `walias` aborts an
    18	//!     in-flight write with EINVAL; an invalid `read` is dropped with
    19	//!     no response since reads have no error status.
